# 1. What do all the methods (move(), special_move(), use()) in the previous activities have in common?
# All these methods have the same purpose of performing an action, but they can produce different results depending 
# on the object using them. They allow different classes to use the same method name even if they perform different actions. 

# 2. How does this activity show polymorphism in a gaming context?
# This activity shows polymorphism because different game characters can perform their own special moves using the 
# same method name, special_move(). For example, a Warrior swings a sword, a Mage casts a spell, and an Archer shoots an arrow. 
# Even though they use the same method, each character has a different action.

